{"id":"canteen-bottle","slug":"canteen-bottle","name":"Canteen (bottle)","aliases":["Field bottle","Water canteen","Canteen (water container)"],"kind":"gear","category":"equipment","subcategory":"Reusable type of water bottle","description":"A canteen is a reusable drinking water bottle designed to be used by hikers, campers, soldiers, bush firefighters, and workers in the field. It is usually fitted with a shoulder strap or means for fastening it to a belt, and may be covered with a cloth bag and padding to protect the bottle and insulate the contents. If the padding is soaked with water, evaporative cooling can help keep the contents of the bottle cool. Many canteens also include a nested canteen cup.","facts":[],"specifications":[],"specIndex":{},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Military_Canteen_7984.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Military_Canteen_7984.jpg","width":3000,"height":1798,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Ashley Pomeroy"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Military_Canteen_7984.jpg/330px-Military_Canteen_7984.jpg"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Military_Canteen_7984.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Military_Canteen_7984.jpg","width":3000,"height":1798,"caption":"A military canteen","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Ashley Pomeroy"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/Alamannic_Canteen.JPG","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alamannic_Canteen.JPG","width":1536,"height":2048,"caption":"Wooden canteen from the alamannic graveyard Oberflacht near Tuttlingen, Germany, 7th century AD. Photographed at Württembergisches Landesmuseum, Stuttgart, Germany","license":"CC BY 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativ